name: Custom.Atlas.WinDnsQuery
description: |
  Atlas-managed (Windows): stream DNS queries from Sysmon Event ID 22
  (DNSEvent) via watch_evtx. Per-query dedup keeps the raw alert volume to one
  per distinct domain; the Python-side Behavior.DnsAnomaly rule scores these
  rows for DGA-like entropy and per-process query bursts.

  DNS is Windows-only here: Velociraptor has no dependable Linux DNS event
  source (no Sysmon-for-Linux DNS provider), so we document the gap rather than
  emit a Linux detector that silently never fires.

  Requires: sysmon (with DNS query logging enabled, schemaversion ≥ 4.1).

type: CLIENT_EVENT

parameters:
  - name: SysmonChannel
    description: Sysmon operational event-log channel.
    default: Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational

sources:
  - query: |
      SELECT
        System.TimeCreated.SystemTime AS timestamp_utc,
        EventData.QueryName AS query_name,
        EventData.QueryResults AS query_results,
        EventData.Image AS image_path,
        atoi(string=EventData.ProcessId) AS pid
      FROM watch_evtx(filename=SysmonChannel, accessor="event_log")
      WHERE System.EventID.Value = 22
        AND query_name != ""
        AND NOT query_name =~ "(?i)\\.(in-addr\\.arpa|ip6\\.arpa|local|localdomain)$"
